[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
     The [1mdf[0m utility displays statistics about the amount of free disk space
     on the specified mounted [4mfile[24m [4msystem[24m or on the file system of which [4mfile[24m
     is a part.  By default block counts are displayed with an assumed block
     size of 512 bytes.  If neither a file or a file system operand is
     specified, statistics for all mounted file systems are displayed
     (subject to the [1m-t[0m option below).

     The following options are available:

     [1m--libxo[0m
             Generate output via libxo(3) in a selection of different human
             and machine readable formats.  See xo_parse_args(3) for details
             on command line arguments.

     [1m-a[0m      Show all mount points, including those that were mounted with
             the MNT_IGNORE flag.  This is implied for file systems specified
             on the command line.

     [1m-b[0m      Explicitly use 512 byte blocks, overriding any BLOCKSIZE
             specification from the environment.  This is the same as the [1m-P[0m
             option.  The [1m-k[0m option overrides this option.

     [1m-c[0m      Display a grand total.

     [1m-g[0m      Use 1073741824 byte (1 Gibibyte) blocks rather than the default.
             This overrides any BLOCKSIZE specification from the environment.

